            "exit": null,
            "emphasis": null,
            "motion": null,
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "• Inside a button two metal contacts touch — and rattle for a few milliseconds\n• The board reads thousands of times a second, so it sees 1, 0, 1, 0, 1 for one press\n• That is contact bounce; every real button does it\n• The fix is in software: count a press only when the reading goes from 0 to 1, and ignore changes shorter than about 20 ms",
            "fill": "none",
            "style": {
              "font": "body",
              "family": "",
              "letterSpacing": 0,
              "size": 40,
              "weight": 400,
              "italic": false,
              "color": "text",
              "align": "left",
              "valign": "top",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fit": "shrink"
            },
            "sizeDriver": null,
            "along": null
          }
        ],
